{%- comment -%}
  YMAL — the theme's own product card, for rows built in the browser.

  Fetched as /products/<handle>?view=ymal-block. Returns one `product-block` and
  nothing else - the SAME card the server-rendered YMAL row uses, so a row
  assembled in the browser (Inspired By Your Views) looks like every other
  product row on the site and follows the theme when it is restyled.

  Why not snippets/ymal-card.liquid: that bespoke card has no styles anywhere in
  the theme any more. They lived in the original custom widget, which was
  replaced by a copy of the theme's product-list section. Reusing it would have
  rendered a bare unstyled list.

  Carries the same eligibility gate as every other YMAL card. An ineligible
  product renders as an empty string and the script skips it - stock and
  *SALE* can change between the source list being fetched and this card being
  fetched, so the check is repeated here rather than trusted.

  no_quick_buy_markup: the theme wires quick buy on page load, and a card
  injected later would show a button that does nothing. The card still links
  to the product.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% layout none %}
{%- liquid
  assign ymal_is_sale = false
  if product.title contains '*SALE*'
    assign ymal_is_sale = true
  endif

  if product.available and product.metafields.ymal.eligible.value and ymal_is_sale == false
    comment
      The same aspect-ratio mapping ymal-widget.liquid uses, for one card. The
      fixed shapes are theme settings; "natural" and "tallest" fall back to the
      product's own image, since there is no row here to measure against.
    endcomment
    if settings.prod_thumb_shape == 'portrait-23'
      assign ymal_ratio = 0.67
    elsif settings.prod_thumb_shape == 'portrait-45'
      assign ymal_ratio = 0.8
    elsif settings.prod_thumb_shape == 'square'
      assign ymal_ratio = 1.0
    elsif settings.prod_thumb_shape == 'landscape-54'
      assign ymal_ratio = 1.25
    elsif settings.prod_thumb_shape == 'landscape-32'
      assign ymal_ratio = 1.50
    else
      assign ymal_ratio = product.featured_media.preview_image.aspect_ratio | default: 1.0
    endif

    render 'product-block', product: product, custom_aspect_ratio: ymal_ratio, no_swiping: true, no_quick_buy_markup: true
  endif
-%}
